#: source/development/experimental-features.md:1
msgid ""
"This section describes the notion of _experimental features_, and how it "
"fits into the big picture of the development of Nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:3
msgid "What are experimental features?"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:5
msgid ""
"Experimental features are considered unstable, which means that they can be "
"changed or removed at any time. Users must explicitly enable them by "
"toggling the associated [experimental feature flags](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-experimental-features). This allows accessing unstable "
"functionality without unwittingly relying on it."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:9
msgid ""
"Experimental feature flags were first introduced in [Nix 2.4](../release-"
"notes/rl-2.4.md). Before that, Nix did have experimental features, but they "
"were not guarded by flags and were merely documented as unstable. This was a "
"source of confusion and controversy."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:13
msgid "When should a new feature be marked experimental?"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:15
msgid ""
"A change in the Nix codebase should be guarded by an experimental feature "
"flag if it is considered likely to be reverted or adapted in a backwards-"
"incompatible manner after gathering more experience with it in practice."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:17
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:19
msgid ""
"Changes to the Nix language, such as new built-ins, syntactic or semantic "
"changes, etc."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:20
msgid "Changes to the command-line interface"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:22
msgid "Lifecycle of an experimental feature"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:24
msgid ""
"Experimental features have to be treated on a case-by-case basis. However, "
"the standard workflow for an experimental feature is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:27
msgid "A new feature is implemented in a _pull request_"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:28
msgid ""
"It is guarded by an experimental feature flag that is disabled by default"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:29
msgid ""
"The pull request is merged, the _experimental_ feature ends up in a release"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:30
msgid ""
"Using the feature requires explicitly enabling it, signifying awareness of "
"the potential risks"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:31
msgid "Being experimental, the feature can still be changed arbitrarily"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:32
msgid "The feature can be _removed_"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:33
msgid "The associated experimental feature flag is also removed"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:34
msgid "The feature can be declared _stable_"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:35
msgid "The associated experimental feature flag is removed"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:36
msgid ""
"There should be enough evidence of users having tried the feature, such as "
"feedback, fixed bugs, demonstrations of how it is put to use"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:37
msgid "Maintainers must feel confident that:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:38
msgid ""
"The feature is designed and implemented sensibly, that it is fit for purpose"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:39
msgid "Potential interactions are well-understood"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:40
msgid ""
"Stabilising the feature will not incur an outsized maintenance burden in the "
"future"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:42
msgid "The following diagram illustrates the process:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:80
msgid "Relation to the RFC process"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:82
msgid ""
"Experimental features and [RFCs](https://github.com/NixOS/rfcs/) both allow "
"approaching substantial changes while minimizing the risk. However they "
"serve different purposes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:85
msgid ""
"An experimental feature enables developers to iterate on and deliver a new "
"idea without committing to it or requiring a costly long-running fork. It is "
"primarily an issue of _implementation_, targeting Nix developers and early "
"testers."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:87
msgid ""
"The goal of an RFC is to make explicit all the implications of a change: "
"Explain why it is wanted, which new use-cases it enables, which interface "
"changes it requires, etc. It is primarily an issue of _design_ and "
"_communication_, targeting the broader community."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:91
msgid ""
"This means that experimental features and RFCs are orthogonal mechanisms, "
"and can be used independently or together as needed."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:93
msgid "Currently available experimental features"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:95
msgid "\\[`auto-allocate-uids`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:97
msgid ""
"Allows Nix to automatically pick UIDs for builds, rather than creating "
"`nixbld*` user accounts. See the [`auto-allocate-uids`](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-auto-allocate-uids) setting for details."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:100
msgid ""
"Refer to [auto-allocate-uids tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/34) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:102
msgid "\\[`blake3-hashes`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:104
msgid "Enables support for BLAKE3 hashes."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:106
msgid ""
"Refer to [blake3-hashes tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/60) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:108
msgid "\\[`ca-derivations`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:110
msgid ""
"Allow derivations to be content-addressed in order to prevent rebuilds when "
"changes to the derivation do not result in changes to the derivation's "
"output. See [\\_\\_contentAddressed](../language/advanced-attributes.md#adv-"
"attr-__contentAddressed) for details."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:116
msgid ""
"Refer to [ca-derivations tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/35) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:118
msgid "\\[`cgroups`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:120
msgid ""
"Allows Nix to execute builds inside cgroups. See the [`use-cgroups`](../"
"command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-use-cgroups) setting for details."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:123
msgid ""
"Refer to [cgroups tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/milestone/36) "
"for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:125
msgid "\\[`configurable-impure-env`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:127
msgid ""
"Allow the use of the [impure-env](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-impure-"
"env) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:129
msgid ""
"Refer to [configurable-impure-env tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/milestone/37) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:131
msgid "\\[`daemon-trust-override`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:133
msgid ""
"Allow forcing trusting or not trusting clients with `nix-daemon`. This is "
"useful for testing, but possibly also useful for various experiments with "
"`nix-daemon --stdio` networking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:138
msgid ""
"Refer to [daemon-trust-override tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/38) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:140
msgid "\\[`dynamic-derivations`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:142
msgid "Allow the use of a few things related to dynamic derivations:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:144
msgid "\"text hashing\" derivation outputs, so we can build .drv files."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:147
msgid ""
"dependencies in derivations on the outputs of derivations that are "
"themselves derivations outputs."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:150
msgid ""
"Refer to [dynamic-derivations tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/39) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:152
msgid "\\[`external-builders`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:154
msgid "Enables support for external builders / sandbox providers."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:156
msgid ""
"Refer to [external-builders tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/62) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:158
msgid "\\[`fetch-closure`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:160
msgid ""
"Enable the use of the [`fetchClosure`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-"
"fetchClosure) built-in function in the Nix language."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:162
msgid ""
"Refer to [fetch-closure tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/40) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:164
msgid "\\[`fetch-tree`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:166
msgid ""
"Enable the use of the [`fetchTree`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-"
"fetchTree) built-in function in the Nix language."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:168
msgid ""
"`fetchTree` exposes a generic interface for fetching remote file system "
"trees from different types of remote sources. The [`flakes`](#xp-feature-"
"flakes) feature flag always enables `fetch-tree`. This built-in was "
"previously guarded by the `flakes` experimental feature because of that "
"overlap."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:172
msgid ""
"Enabling just this feature serves as a \"release candidate\", allowing users "
"to try it out in isolation."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:174
msgid ""
"Refer to [fetch-tree tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/31) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:176
msgid "\\[`flakes`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:178
msgid ""
"Enable flakes. See the manual entry for [`nix flake`](../command-ref/new-cli/"
"nix3-flake.md) for details."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:181
msgid ""
"Refer to [flakes tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/milestone/27) "
"for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:183
msgid "\\[`git-hashing`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:185
msgid ""
"Allow creating (content-addressed) store objects which are hashed via Git's "
"hashing algorithm. These store objects aren't understandable by older "
"versions of Nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:188
msgid ""
"Refer to [git-hashing tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/41) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:190
msgid "\\[`impure-derivations`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:192
msgid ""
"Allow derivations to produce non-fixed outputs by setting the `__impure` "
"derivation attribute to `true`. An impure derivation can have differing "
"outputs each time it is built."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:196
#: source/development/experimental-features.md:261
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:198
msgid ""
"```\n"
"derivation {\n"
"  name = \"impure\";\n"
"  builder = /bin/sh;\n"
"  __impure = true; # mark this derivation as impure\n"
"  args = [ \"-c\" \"read -n 10 random < /dev/random; echo $random > "
"$out\" ];\n"
"  system = builtins.currentSystem;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:208
msgid ""
"Each time this derivation is built, it can produce a different output (as "
"the builder outputs random bytes to `$out`).  Impure derivations also have "
"access to the network, and only fixed-output or other impure derivations can "
"rely on impure derivations. Finally, an impure derivation cannot also be "
"[content-addressed](#xp-feature-ca-derivations)."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:215
msgid ""
"This is a more explicit alternative to using [`builtins.currentTime`](../"
"language/builtins.md#builtins-currentTime)."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:217
msgid ""
"Refer to [impure-derivations tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/42) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:219
msgid "\\[`local-overlay-store`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:221
msgid ""
"Allow the use of [local overlay store](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-"
"stores.md#experimental-local-overlay-store)."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:223
msgid ""
"Refer to [local-overlay-store tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/50) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:225
msgid "\\[`mounted-ssh-store`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:227
msgid ""
"Allow the use of the [`mounted SSH store`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-"
"stores.html#experimental-ssh-store-with-filesystem-mounted)."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:229
msgid ""
"Refer to [mounted-ssh-store tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/43) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:231
msgid "\\[`nix-command`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:233
msgid ""
"Enable the new `nix` subcommands. See the manual on [`nix`](../command-ref/"
"new-cli/nix.md) for details."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:236
msgid ""
"Refer to [nix-command tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/28) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:238
msgid "\\[`parse-toml-timestamps`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:240
msgid "Allow parsing of timestamps in builtins.fromTOML."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:242
msgid ""
"Refer to [parse-toml-timestamps tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/45) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:244
msgid "\\[`pipe-operators`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:246
msgid "Add `|>` and `<|` operators to the Nix language."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:248
msgid ""
"Refer to [pipe-operators tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/55) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:250
msgid "\\[`read-only-local-store`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:252
msgid ""
"Allow the use of the `read-only` parameter in [local store](../store/types/"
"local-store.md) URIs."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:254
msgid ""
"Refer to [read-only-local-store tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/46) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:256
msgid "\\[`recursive-nix`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:258
msgid ""
"Allow derivation builders to call Nix, and thus build derivations "
"recursively."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:263
msgid ""
"```\n"
"with import <nixpkgs> {};\n"
"\n"
"runCommand \"foo\"\n"
"  {\n"
"     # Optional: let Nix know \"foo\" requires the experimental feature\n"
"     requiredSystemFeatures = [ \"recursive-nix\" ];\n"
"     buildInputs = [ nix jq ];\n"
"     NIX_PATH = \"nixpkgs=${<nixpkgs>}\";\n"
"  }\n"
"  ''\n"
"    hello=$(nix-build -E '(import <nixpkgs> {}).hello.overrideDerivation "
"(args: { name = \"recursive-hello\"; })')\n"
"\n"
"    mkdir -p $out/bin\n"
"    ln -s $hello/bin/hello $out/bin/hello\n"
"  ''\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:281
msgid ""
"An important restriction on recursive builders is disallowing arbitrary "
"substitutions. For example, running"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:288
msgid ""
"in the above `runCommand` script would be disallowed, as this could lead to "
"derivations with hidden dependencies or breaking reproducibility by relying "
"on the current state of the Nix store. An exception would be if `/nix/store/"
"lrs9qfm60jcgsk83qhyypj3m4jqsgdid-hello-2.10` were already in the build "
"inputs or built by a previous recursive Nix call."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:296
msgid ""
"Refer to [recursive-nix tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/47) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:298
msgid "\\[`verified-fetches`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:300
msgid ""
"Enables verification of git commit signatures through the [`fetchGit`](../"
"language/builtins.md#builtins-fetchGit) built-in."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/experimental-features.md:302
msgid ""
"Refer to [verified-fetches tracking issue](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"milestone/48) for feature tracking."
msgstr ""
